  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Egypt &#x2013; Processing (Organic) Peanuts</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">With a DGGF loan Katjang Jerry BV will be able to, together with its partners, expand working capital and production capacity.Kernile for Trade and Export LLC was established as a joint venture between the Dutch Katjang Group and the Egyptian Growtech SAE. The Katjang group is a producer of roasted and coated nuts, Growtech is an agricultural company and exporter of fleece peanuts, seeds, fertilzers and agrochemicals. Kernile was founded with the support of the PSI program of RVO in 2016. Kernile focuses on the sourcing, processing and supply of peanut products for the European and MENA markets in particular. In addition, Kernile also partially provides work for third parties. The establishment of Kernile has the advantage that Katjang has access to reliable raw materials, for Growtech Kernile gives access to the market in Europe. Due to the results in recent years and the expected growth for the coming years, there is a need for additional expansion of working capital and production capacity. The investment underscores Kernile&apos;s strategic orientation to focus on the organic market, the blanched peanut market and food safety. Investment consists of the purchase of the land, building and machinery. The machines in which investments are made include a blanching machine, but also machines to improve food safety and meet the requirements that organic production entails. Through this funding, impact is realized by creating additional employment (+39 jobs in 5 years) and increasing productive power (+ 8,740 MT in 5 years). Indirect impact is the sourcing and training of supplying farmers (+/ 1400) and the production of reliable food.</narrative>
  </description>
